From 4653c6c210e796b2f8023967a7b93129857ceeff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 03:25:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] claude_code_ide, zed: rustfmt the story-001 hand-written
 code

These were the last files failing `cargo fmt --check` on this fork. Both are
hand-written rather than upstream: the claude_code_ide crate arrived as a
manually applied overlay patch, and zed.rs had its ReleaseChannel::Stable match
arm expanded into a block when the Zeo arm was added beside it -- rustfmt wants
it back as a one-liner.

Layout only. Every string and numeric literal is byte-identical before and after.
The fork now passes `cargo fmt --check` in full, which keeps it from drifting
against upstream's own fmt gate at rebase time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
